  "notes": "Fixed-text design: translation text is repeats[0]'s final cumulative text, held constant across both prompt variants and across the 2 judge-repeats within each variant -- only the judge call varies, isolating judge-scoring noise from translation-generation stochasticity (a known conflation in cycle 19-21's existing noise-floor baseline, which called judge() once per separately-generated translation repeat). within_group_noise_stdev is sqrt(mean(per-group variance)), matching judge_noise_power_analysis.py's _decompose_zero_effect_variance() within-group convention. A negative mean_delta_reasoning_minus_score_first supports rubriceval2603's reasoning-before-score finding generalizing to this task; report honestly if the difference is small relative to either variant's own noise, since this is a single K=2 check, not a well-powered test."
